    "summary": "Sample of adire dyeing using a single width of imported European calico cotton. The cloth shows two stages of the production. One end (with a drawstring) remains undyed but has been stitched with rows of closely-tied circles, each containing a bean or suchlike. The other end shows the pattern of small &#039;flowers&#039; resulting from this stitching after the cloth has been indigo-dyed and unstitched. The central section of the cloth is untouched, raw calico.",
